                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bd877a58-085c-3976-9724-34b5af2dde32",
                        "entry_id": "715de7b7-dc56-30cf-9cc8-43183f36f37d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Gewebsuntergang durch eine Unterversorgung mit Sauerstoff als Folge einer unzureichenden oder unterbrochenen Durchblutung"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cea1b19c-b7b9-43d6-a64e-9007bdaec754",
                                "sense_id": "bd877a58-085c-3976-9724-34b5af2dde32",
                                "text": "„Die Implantation von körpereigenen Muskelzellen könnte auch beim Menschen eine erfolgversprechende Therapieform bei Infarkten sein, hoffen die Wissenschaftler.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ef67f6f6-01c1-4fdf-99aa-cd6467bc2728",
                        "source_entry_id": "715de7b7-dc56-30cf-9cc8-43183f36f37d",
                        "source_sense_id": "bd877a58-085c-3976-9724-34b5af2dde32",
                        "target_lang_word": "infarction",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "infarction",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "634a3329-315d-34b1-a2bd-080492197189",
                                        "entry_id": "2c166d39-a24a-3ba1-b60e-d235dc8a03e1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The process which causes an infarct."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae23c66b-a970-394d-92c2-08530eaebbfc",
                                        "entry_id": "2c166d39-a24a-3ba1-b60e-d235dc8a03e1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An infarct (an area of ischemic necrosis)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55e0a783-5f3a-4d51-b0da-0b1eed261129",
                                                "sense_id": "ae23c66b-a970-394d-92c2-08530eaebbfc",
                                                "text": "But we can no longer regard the mere fact of these diffuse condensations of the lung becoming yellow and caseous as an evidence of their tuberculous nature, especially since the pathological anatomists, and among them Virchow, have shown that formations of the most different kind, having not the slightest connection with tubercule— as, for example, old cancerous masses, lymphatic glands swollen by a hyperplasia of cells, hæmorrhagical infarctions, abscesses, &c.— undergo exactly the same caseous transformation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc0e0320-caf2-43ce-b109-df256f140881",
                                                "sense_id": "ae23c66b-a970-394d-92c2-08530eaebbfc",
                                                "text": "Once stroke was classified by a risk factor-free method, the stronger relationship between hypertension and lacunar versus nonlacunar infarction patients disappeared."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8b486abd-7353-42ec-a0b6-1ab8de11df5e",
                        "source_entry_id": "715de7b7-dc56-30cf-9cc8-43183f36f37d",
                        "source_sense_id": "bd877a58-085c-3976-9724-34b5af2dde32",
                        "target_lang_word": "infarctus",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "infarctus",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e8da5c5d-775c-3f2a-88cd-ae12c03c232e",
                                        "entry_id": "93140a0b-3798-3737-b484-f8015079efbf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lésion nécrotique de certains tissus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21e4e730-f638-460f-9548-ff67c3860bbe",
                                                "sense_id": "e8da5c5d-775c-3f2a-88cd-ae12c03c232e",
                                                "text": "Excusez mon retard. Il est dû (vous ne le devineriez jamais) à un… infarctus du myocarde (ce fameux infarctus à la mode) que rien ne laissait prévoir, qu’aucune fatigue n’annonçait et dont je suis en train de me remettre au bout de ce mois de mars passé dans une clinique toulousaine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25393a8e-6bc9-4155-a05e-ff2eaf8ce9b8",
                                                "sense_id": "e8da5c5d-775c-3f2a-88cd-ae12c03c232e",
                                                "text": "Imaginez qu’une injection permette de reconstituer du tissu myocardique en quelques heures, on sauverait quatre-vingt-dix pour cent des infarctus…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bd8db01-1de5-4817-96fb-590dfd4cb259",
                                                "sense_id": "e8da5c5d-775c-3f2a-88cd-ae12c03c232e",
                                                "text": "Pour montrer à quel point la COVID engorge le système et draine des ressources, le docteur Simon a utilisé une image claire.\n «Un infarctus, c’est deux, trois jours aux soins intensifs. Si vous venez pour une pneumonie, c’est six jours. La COVID, c’est 14 jours.»"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
